WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.295 --> 00:00:02.594
- I predict pain, tears.

00:00:02.594 --> 00:00:04.602
- Chili chips are not
big at all in Australia,

00:00:04.602 --> 00:00:05.334
I'd say.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:07.238
- We don't really have
the extreme flavors.

00:00:07.238 --> 00:00:08.178
- I think it's gonna be easy.

00:00:08.178 --> 00:00:09.280
I think I'm gonna smash it.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.782
(rock music)

00:00:20.136 --> 00:00:22.214
- Ah, yeah, I was gonna
say it's not very hot,

00:00:22.214 --> 00:00:24.373
and then it goes down and it is quite hot.

00:00:24.373 --> 00:00:25.093
- Oh, there it is.

00:00:25.093 --> 00:00:26.439
- I hate chili and that wasn't even bad,

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:27.218
that's very mild.

00:00:27.218 --> 00:00:29.980
- It tastes like chili and
lemon lollies or something.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.499
- Yeah, like chili and
lemon washing-up detergent.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.891
(rock music)

00:00:34.891 --> 00:00:35.820
- [Voiceover] Tastes like a Dorito.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:36.993
- Like a stale Dorito.

00:00:36.993 --> 00:00:37.758
- Oh yeah.

00:00:37.758 --> 00:00:39.094
- Yeah, I like that.

00:00:39.094 --> 00:00:40.359
- That was good, it was too small.

00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:41.438
- It's like one of those where you just

00:00:41.438 --> 00:00:42.820
want to fill your whole mouth with,

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.237
and go crazy with, like a Pringle.

00:00:44.237 --> 00:00:45.375
- Yeah, I can see myself stuffing

00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:47.058
big fistfuls of that into my face.

00:00:47.058 --> 00:00:47.836
- Not spicy.

00:00:47.836 --> 00:00:48.938
- Not much chili flavor.

00:00:48.938 --> 00:00:49.891
- No chili flavor.

00:00:49.891 --> 00:00:53.060
(rock music)

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.336
- Tastes like a 99 cent
burrito from Taco Bell,

00:00:55.336 --> 00:00:56.253
and I love it.

00:00:56.253 --> 00:00:57.459
- They kind of hurt me.

00:00:57.459 --> 00:00:58.678
- That's definitely spicy.

00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:00.513
- That tastes like my
mouth after a night out.

00:01:00.513 --> 00:01:01.418
- Can't stop eating them.

00:01:01.418 --> 00:01:05.221
(rock music)

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:07.920
- Woah, that doesn't look like the

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.813
color of something that
should go in your mouth.

00:01:09.813 --> 00:01:10.532
- No.

00:01:10.532 --> 00:01:12.296
- I don't even think that color exists.

00:01:12.296 --> 00:01:13.597
- It's built to nothing.

00:01:13.597 --> 00:01:16.813
- Like air wrapped in flavor red.

00:01:16.813 --> 00:01:18.496
- It's like a bad Twistie.

00:01:18.496 --> 00:01:19.738
A Twistie that lost its way.

00:01:19.738 --> 00:01:22.257
- It's burning the back of my mouth

00:01:22.257 --> 00:01:23.554
at the moment, and that was one.

00:01:23.554 --> 00:01:24.289
- Mm.

00:01:24.289 --> 00:01:26.456
- So I'm not going in for a handful.

00:01:26.456 --> 00:01:29.765
(rock music)

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.276
- [Voiceover] (laughs) What is this?

00:01:33.276 --> 00:01:35.888
- This looks like a little
bit of rolled-up meat.

00:01:35.888 --> 00:01:37.049
- That looks like a salami stick.

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:38.547
- Pure chili.

00:01:38.547 --> 00:01:39.777
- You should not put more than

00:01:39.777 --> 00:01:41.008
one of these into you.

00:01:41.008 --> 00:01:42.715
- Mm-mm.

00:01:42.715 --> 00:01:43.748
- No.

00:01:43.748 --> 00:01:45.071
- I think it would be great with a beer.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:48.492
- Tastes like off, hot, chili cheese.

00:01:48.492 --> 00:01:50.272
- Probably the perfect amount of chili.

00:01:50.272 --> 00:01:51.909
- Feel like I've just been
punched in the throat.

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:54.458
(rock music)

00:01:55.995 --> 00:01:57.691
- [Voiceover] They're
kind of a smoky chili,

00:01:57.691 --> 00:01:59.351
or no chili, just smoky.

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:03.031
- It's like a barbecue
flavor style, but then

00:02:03.031 --> 00:02:05.074
now the heat is coming and again,

00:02:05.074 --> 00:02:06.348
my mouth's on fire.

00:02:06.348 --> 00:02:07.904
- It tastes really bacony.

00:02:07.904 --> 00:02:08.520
- Yeah.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.924
- It's like a cheese and bacon bowl

00:02:09.924 --> 00:02:11.039
but quite subtle.

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:14.749
(rock music)

00:02:17.528 --> 00:02:19.049
- [Voiceover] Funyuns,
I've heard about Funyuns!

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:20.083
- [Voiceover] So have I!

00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:21.220
- [Voiceover] That'd be
good with sour cream.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.008
- Yeah, or guac.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:25.248
- I like the texture,
it was soft and fluffy.

00:02:25.248 --> 00:02:27.988
- They taste like nothing, but crunch.

00:02:27.988 --> 00:02:29.648
- It really is a Funyun.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:32.238
(rock music)

00:02:32.238 --> 00:02:34.060
- I think these ones they certainly

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.126
look a lot scarier than they taste.

00:02:36.126 --> 00:02:37.741
- I'm supportive of chili flavored chips.

00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:39.540
I think we need more of them here.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.186
Australia hasn't embraced
the chili chip yet.

00:02:42.186 --> 00:02:42.911
But we should.

